Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Human OS project <noreply@humanhealthos.invalid>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgtk-3-0t64 | libgtk-3-0, libglib2.0-0t64 | libglib2.0-0, libatk1.0-0t64 | libatk1.0-0, libcairo2, libcairo-gobject2, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0, libpango-1.0-0, libpangocairo-1.0-0, libharfbuzz0b, libfontconfig1, libepoxy0, libegl1, libgles2, libgl1, libstdc++6, libgcc-s1, zlib1g
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/kaansavukduran/human-os
Description: Human OS personal health record
 Offline-first personal health record built with Flutter: measurements,
 labs as printed, medicines, sleep, food, activity and more, each with its
 source and history. Development builds keep a clearly labelled unencrypted
 log in your data folder and must not hold real health data; staging and
 production builds keep everything in an encrypted vault that opens with your
 passphrase. Not for clinical decisions. No network access.
